        One verifies the Leibniz rule and that the curvature is indeed given by $2\pi \mathbf{i} \omega_K(L)$. For the final statement we note that $\omega_K(L)$ differs from $\frac{1}{2}\omega_K $ by $\frac{1}{2}\begin{pmatrix}
